# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nahhas Field Engineer Portal — environment
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and set VITE_API_BASE for the environment you are
# pointing at. Only ONE variable is needed. Vite only exposes vars prefixed
# with VITE_ to the browser, and the value is baked in at BUILD time — so a
# production build must be made with the production value present.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT (default — talk to a local Odoo instance).
# Match the port your local Odoo actually listens on (8069 is the Odoo
# default; use 8019 if that is how your instance is configured).
#
# The Vite dev server runs on :5173, so these calls are cross-origin. The
# API's default `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` covers this — no proxy is
# used, so local behaves exactly like production.
#
# PREREQUISITE on the Odoo side: the server must resolve to ONE database on
# its own, or it answers 404 "No database is selected" before the route runs
# and the browser reports it as a CORS failure. Set `db_name = <your db>` in
# odoo.conf — see odoo.conf.example in the Nahhas-Group repo. There is no
# client-side fix: a browser cannot send the `X-Odoo-Database` header.
VITE_API_BASE=http://localhost:8019/api/field_portal/v1

# LAN TESTING on a real phone. The phone cannot resolve "localhost", so use
# the machine's LAN IP for both the dev server and the API.
# VITE_API_BASE=http://192.168.1.50:8019/api/field_portal/v1

# PRODUCTION — app served from https://site.nahas.group, API on erp.nahas.group.
# Different origins, so CORS applies; `erp.nahas.group` already resolves its
# own database by host, so nothing extra is needed. Optionally narrow the API's
# allowed origin by setting FIELD_PORTAL_CORS_ORIGIN=https://site.nahas.group
# in the Odoo server's environment. See DEPLOYMENT.md.
# VITE_API_BASE=https://erp.nahas.group/api/field_portal/v1
